{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["Or with a fist (אוֹ בְאֶגְרֹף) — according to the plain sense: as its Targum [renders it], a kind of stone or brick, for Scripture speaks of the throwing of a stone. And so I found in Torat Kohanim, in the section on plague-affections of houses, at וְחָלְצוּ הָאֲבָנִים — 'in bricks or [in turmisin].' And likewise: to strike with a fist (באגרוף) means 'wickedly' — with a large stone by which one might kill or inflict injury."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The word טורמסין in brackets appears to be a textual addition or variant; it seems to refer to a type of building material (possibly tufa/porous stone). The final sentence about 'wickedly' (רשע) puns on reading אגרוף as related to רשע, interpreting the phrase להכות באגרוף רשע as 'to strike wickedly with a large stone.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:26.082709229Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}